<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Carabobo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1821</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venezuelan-war-of-independence">Venezuelan War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Carabobo was fought on 24 June 1821 south-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>, Venezuela. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a>'s patriot army defeated the royalist forces of Miguel de la Torre, with the British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> playing a notable part. The victory secured Venezuelan independence; the last Spanish garrison held out at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-cabello">Puerto Cabello</a> until 1823.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-carabobo.jpg" alt="Battle of Carabobo" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BatallaCarabobo01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
